records.rationale:
In `create_account_controller.js`, previously rejected emails are short-circuited with a hardcoded reason `I18n.t('user.email.invalid')`:
```js
if (this.get('rejectedEmails').contains(email)) {
  return Discourse.InputValidation.create({ failed: true, reason: I18n.t('user.email.invalid') });
}
```
But the server-side validator can specifically add `I18n.t(:'user.email.blocked')` when `BlockedEmail.should_block?(value)` is true (`lib/validators/email_validator.rb`). The server also now returns structured `errors` and `values`, and the client caches rejected emails whenever `result.errors.email`

